---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const lang = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Science — Activist Resiliency"
  description="The research and contemplative wisdom grounding this site — polyvagal theory, window of tolerance, climate resilience science, and contemplative traditions."
  lang={lang}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-title">The Science</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">
        This site draws on a foundation of peer-reviewed research and tested
        contemplative wisdom. Understanding the science behind stress, nervous
        system regulation, and resilience can itself be a tool — it helps
        activists make sense of their own experience and choose practices with
        intention. Below are the four pillars of the research grounding this work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="topics-section">
    <div class="container topics-grid">
      <a href="/en/science/polyvagal" class="topic-card topic-polyvagal">
        <div class="topic-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9762;</div>
        <h2 class="topic-title">Polyvagal Theory</h2>
        <p class="topic-author">Stephen Porges</p>
        <p class="topic-description">
          How the autonomic nervous system governs safety, mobilization, and
          shutdown — and why connection is the nervous system's first resource.
        </p>
        <span class="topic-link">Explore &rarr;</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/en/science/window-of-tolerance" class="topic-card topic-window">
        <div class="topic-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9651;</div>
        <h2 class="topic-title">Window of Tolerance</h2>
        <p class="topic-author">Dan Siegel</p>
        <p class="topic-description">
          The optimal zone of arousal where you can think clearly, feel fully,
          and respond flexibly — and how to widen it under sustained pressure.
        </p>
        <span class="topic-link">Explore &rarr;</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/en/science/climate-resilience" class="topic-card topic-climate">
        <div class="topic-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#127758;</div>
        <h2 class="topic-title">Climate &amp; Sustained Resilience</h2>
        <p class="topic-author">Elissa Epel</p>
        <p class="topic-description">
          Stress biology, telomere research, and what science tells us about
          building biological resilience for long-haul activist work.
        </p>
        <span class="topic-link">Explore &rarr;</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/en/science/contemplative" class="topic-card topic-contemplative">
        <div class="topic-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128218;</div>
        <h2 class="topic-title">Contemplative Traditions</h2>
        <p class="topic-author">Mindfulness, Breathwork &amp; IFS</p>
        <p class="topic-description">
          How ancient contemplative practices map onto modern neuroscience — and
          how they build the regulation and integration capacity activists need.
        </p>
        <span class="topic-link">Explore &rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grounding-note">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="note-inner">
        <h2 class="note-heading">Why Science Matters for Activists</h2>
        <p>
          Activist work generates real physiological stress responses. Sustained
          exposure to injustice, threat, and grief is not metaphorical — it
          leaves measurable traces in the body: elevated cortisol, shortened
          telomeres, narrowed windows of tolerance. Understanding this is not
          defeatist. It is the beginning of choosing wisely.
        </p>
        <p>
          The framework underlying this site — Moral Resiliency — synthesizes
          these research traditions with contemplative wisdom. The goal is not
          to eliminate stress (which is impossible and undesirable) but to
          develop the capacity to move through it without collapse, and to
          return again and again to grounded, connected action.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .page-intro {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .topics-section {
    padding: var(--space-lg) 0;
  }

  .topics-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  @media (max-width: 639px) {
    .topics-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .topic-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    border-radius: 12px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: white;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .topic-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
    color: white;
  }

  .topic-polyvagal {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #5a7c6a, #3d5c4e);
  }

  .topic-window {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6a7a8c, #3d5066);
  }

  .topic-climate {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #8c7a5a, #664f2e);
  }

  .topic-contemplative {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #7a5a8c, #4d2e66);
  }

  .topic-icon {
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .topic-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: white;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .topic-author {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .topic-description {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    line-height: 1.6;
    flex: 1;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .topic-link {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .grounding-note {
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .note-inner {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    background-color: var(--color-white);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-sage);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .note-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .note-inner p {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
  }
</style>
